32:14.020 --> 32:19.840
FFS is used to do file-level encryption.

32:19.840 --> 32:30.900
This has the aspect that it works on both NAND storage, Naked NAND, with UB and UBIFS,

32:30.900 --> 32:38.920
as well as on block devices because it works in an upper layer when it's working with

32:38.920 --> 32:41.120
the files.

32:41.120 --> 32:43.960
So every file in the encrypted system,

32:45.560 --> 32:48.360
in the encrypted file system corresponds to a file

32:48.360 --> 32:51.160
in the unencrypted to the lower file system.

32:52.840 --> 32:56.380
