45:26.160 --> 45:27.680
Just for development's sake,

45:27.680 --> 45:30.120
put your development keys in your board support package

45:30.120 --> 45:32.420
that everyone can build a root file system

45:32.420 --> 45:34.560
and a bootloader and just play with it,

45:34.560 --> 45:36.060
every developer that wants to.

45:39.620 --> 45:42.440
The keys that are used in production,

45:42.440 --> 45:47.440
you can not put it into your BSP

45:48.120 --> 45:52.120
because these have to be protected,

45:52.120 --> 45:55.780
but you can make use of cryptographics,

45:55.780 --> 46:04.780
standard API PK-CS11 that all the tools can use to read them.

46:04.780 --> 46:10.480
You can put them on a smart card or even on a hardware security model that's somewhere

46:10.480 --> 46:20.380
on the network or make use of some vendors that have software, hardware security models

46:20.380 --> 46:25.740
that you can access over the internet with complicated schemes or whatever.

46:25.740 --> 46:36.100
And what's really handy for development is that you have some packages in two configuration.

46:36.100 --> 46:37.860
For example, the bootloader.

46:37.860 --> 46:44.840
You want to have the bootloader that you can log into, have shell access, maybe even can

46:44.840 --> 46:53.440
read out the log from the kernel and do booting from NFS root, just that the developers can

46:53.440 --> 46:59.280
work and the guys who want to debug and just have a different bootloader a different bootloader

46:59.280 --> 47:05.840
configuration that's all secured no interaction no state no environment with your production keys

47:06.800 --> 47:12.640
just keep that separate that you can that your developers still can can work and still can be

47:12.640 --> 47:22.640
happy and are not hindered by the bootloader and you can do this also for the kernel maybe one

47:22.640 --> 47:29.440
kernel that reboots as soon as a security violation is detected and another kernel that

47:29.440 --> 47:38.240
just says oh sorry permission denied there was a problem with the security and during integration

47:38.240 --> 47:45.760
what turned out to be really good is that we regularly turn for every release some of the

47:45.760 --> 47:52.260
